 {:db/id "q-105123" :question/id #uuid "2a851309-6577-5c09-b5b9-0e83f2309404" :question/math-academy-id "q-105123" :question/problem "If $T={k,m,o},$ then $P(T)=$" :question/worked-solution "The power set of $T,$ denoted $P(T),$ is the set that contains every possible subset of $T,$ including the empty set $∅.$\n\nSo, let's list all possible subsets of $T$ using a tree diagram.\n\n![](images/1e/1ef8e646081305399cddbf6908bd8415d908dab3e9bb0e371d68b33e62084774.png)\n\nAccording to our diagram, the subsets of $T$ are\n\n$$\n∅={},\\,{k},\\,{m},\\,{o},\\,{k,m},\\,{k,o},\\,{m,o},\\,{k,m,o}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(T)={∅,{k},{m},{o},{k,m},{k,o},{m,o},{k,m,o}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-105123/ma-source-field/d892506ed61f3017cf6e12eba7463250e83a39505b0cd8759a733908a112d30e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
