 {:db/id "q-1203" :question/id #uuid "350a2acf-787e-5ee2-949f-2438ca3d2b8a" :question/math-academy-id "q-1203" :question/problem "If $X={2,4,8}$, then $P(X)=$" :question/worked-solution "The power set of $X,$ denoted $P(X),$ is the set that contains every possible subset of $X,$ including the empty set $∅.$\n\nSo, let's list all possible subsets of $X$ using a tree diagram. \n\n![](images/58/580d7c32378a2af641fb1066cec4ec24cc6c5b140ccf9475f9a3e3a68367d30d.png)\n\nAccording to our diagram, the subsets of $X$ are\n\n$$\n∅={},\\,{2},\\,{4},\\,{8},\\,{2,4},\\,{2,8},\\,{4,8},\\,{2,4,8}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(X)={∅,{2},{4},{8},{2,4},{2,8},{4,8},{2,4,8}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-1203/ma-source-field/168f9ea4d7b2307401be3a966a1819e33ab83664c2a7074d3cb312f8c6f9c2cf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
