 {:db/id "q-1208" :question/id #uuid "23e8510c-99c3-539c-9c30-63245db2572b" :question/math-academy-id "q-1208" :question/problem "Which statement is **not** true?" :question/worked-solution "If $A⊆B,$ then $A$ is a subset of $B,$ meaning that every element of $A$ is an element of $B.$\n\nAmong the given choices, only $C⊆Z$ is not true. This statement is not true because not every complex is an integer number. For example, we have $2\\text{i}\\in C$ but $2\\text{i}\\notin Z.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-1208/ma-source-field/82f763aaa0e8334dedf0f46da0f551bc4c351b6a39578c71cf8f37ab01f78ef4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
