 {:db/id "q-1270" :question/id #uuid "6fe130ed-ce3d-5283-a70b-402fc6b51c7c" :question/math-academy-id "q-1270" :question/problem "If $T={2,4,6,8,10}$, which collection of subsets of $T$ is a partition of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "A partition of a set $T$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $T$ where every element of $T$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only ${{2,4,6},{8},{10}}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- ${∅,{2,4},{6,8},{10}}$ is not a partition because the subset $∅$ is empty.\n\n- ${∅,{2,4},{6,8},{8,10}}$ is not a partition because the subset $∅$ is empty.\n\n- ${{2},{4},{6,8}}$ is not a partition because the element $10\\in T$ does not appear in any subset.\n\n- ${{2},{2,4},{6,8,10}}$ is not a partition because the element $2$ appears in two subsets." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-1270/ma-source-field/af446cbcf13db178150e47aaa82382f0275bc885784a2525db6b4a8c24996c71"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
