 {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "7e7b9d16-36b0-577e-a63c-c84d780d74e5"] :question/problem "If $Y={2,4,6,…,100},$ which collection of subsets of $Y$ is a partition of $Y?$" :question/worked-solution "A partition of a set $Y$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $Y$ where every element of $Y$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only ${{2,4,6,…,40},{42,44,46,…,60},{62,64,66,…,100}}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- ${{2,4,6,…,40},{80,82,84,…,100}}$ is not a partition because many elements of $Y$ (such as $42$) do not appear in any subsets.\n\n- ${{2,4,6,…,40},{20,22,24,…,100}}$ is not a partition because many elements (such as $20$) appear in both subsets.\n\n- ${{1,2,3,…,100}}$ is not a partition because it contains many elements (such as $1$) that do not appear in $Y.$\n\n- ${{4,6,8,10},{10,11,12,…,100}}$ is not a partition because it contains many elements (such as $11$) that do not appear in $Y.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-1275/ma-source-field/58b7afc3205aba1a2489abc4d47ec381c55cc3fe2bc8cea371454cb745d09934"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
