 {:db/id "q-13497" :question/id #uuid "d09f8217-b119-5565-bb4f-2ae4305acd87" :question/math-academy-id "q-13497" :question/problem "Find the entry ${c}_{24}$ of the matrix $C$, where \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -3 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The entry ${c}_{24}$ should lie at the intersection of the $2$nd row and $4$th column. Therefore, ${c}_{24}=5.$\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-13497/ma-source-field/18e512fc1475be2a2b38b955cb26b6a286ec7404e1dde3b1121891bea7fa1cc3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
