 {:db/id "q-14191" :question/id #uuid "2a1f70ec-1a84-5f86-99bd-fdd4752087f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-14191" :question/problem "Find the point of intersection of the parabola ${y}^{2}+13x-15y-2=0$ with the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "When the parabola intersects the $x$-axis, we must have $y=0.$ So, we set $y=0$ and solve the resulting equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0)^{2}+13x-15(0)-2 & =0 \\\\ 13x-2 & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{2}{13}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parabola intersects the $x$-axis at $(\\frac{2}{13},0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-14191/ma-source-field/1444459bd1c216dfe49d32e008dbeb3a5ca034bed3b2d4a34e7c7f12286dab0a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
