 {:db/id "q-20512/ma-source-field/d1f0e81af0136c9857cd93c7fb6f101488d8577f3cc6de0b95e882f28d83ad15" :answer-field/id #uuid "2a758e48-dc27-560b-a0af-fd01b7ea572b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-20512/ma-source-field/d1f0e81af0136c9857cd93c7fb6f101488d8577f3cc6de0b95e882f28d83ad15/efaa7bd3d4f8e8110d9bcac6d204f4f88e0de8467ac2ed3c49c58654448589ee" "q-20512/ma-source-field/d1f0e81af0136c9857cd93c7fb6f101488d8577f3cc6de0b95e882f28d83ad15/46996c293a0e5a395194e12cf3aa4eaf1c1ba7c8384710202d2b89162326291b" "q-20512/ma-source-field/d1f0e81af0136c9857cd93c7fb6f101488d8577f3cc6de0b95e882f28d83ad15/d43f2bc3959094d8945e65995fe070d4c5b54544529c2f925c851d0f9149a619" "q-20512/ma-source-field/d1f0e81af0136c9857cd93c7fb6f101488d8577f3cc6de0b95e882f28d83ad15/b28998f32559b8196d6bf761d3b3745c7ddfa2f2372a591f566a3643d60bc3d0" "q-20512/ma-source-field/d1f0e81af0136c9857cd93c7fb6f101488d8577f3cc6de0b95e882f28d83ad15/c51ba793173191e30f05b26d15bcd194e949fe064f36c078cd8064ee1f5e57da"] :answer-field/correct "q-20512/ma-source-field/d1f0e81af0136c9857cd93c7fb6f101488d8577f3cc6de0b95e882f28d83ad15/c51ba793173191e30f05b26d15bcd194e949fe064f36c078cd8064ee1f5e57da" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-20512" :question/id #uuid "3437106d-95df-5058-942b-4f64c5179bc5" :question/math-academy-id "q-20512" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+2z=1 \\\\  & 2x+3y+4z=6 \\\\  & 3x+3y+4z=11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and hence solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 4 & 11\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 4 & 11\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 4 & 11\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+2z=1 \\\\  & y=4 \\\\  & z=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. Substituting both $y=4$ and $z=-4$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+(4)+2(-4)=1\\,⟹\\,x=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=5,y=4$, and $z=-4.$ Or, in vector form, $⟨5,4,-4⟩.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-20512/ma-source-field/d1f0e81af0136c9857cd93c7fb6f101488d8577f3cc6de0b95e882f28d83ad15"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
