 {:db/id "q-2870" :question/id #uuid "a45a10dd-0c29-5839-ade5-5e0193cac871" :question/math-academy-id "q-2870" :question/problem "![](images/59/598fa373c0312c910c1a13b435a35e6745d3c912884b36b208b7c2d4fca42f75.png)\n\nA circle is decreasing in area at a rate of $8\\pi \\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}\\text{/s}.$ Calculate the rate at which the circumference of the circle is decreasing at the moment when the radius is  $5\\,\\text{cm}.$" :question/worked-solution "In this situation, we want to find $\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}$ at the moment when $r=5,$ and we are also told that  $\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=-8\\pi .$\n\nTo start, let's set up an equation relating the area $A$ and the circumference $C$ of the circle. Since $C=2\\pi r$ and $A=\\pi {r}^{2},$ the relationship between $A$ and $C$ is\n\n$$\nA=\\pi {r}^{2}=\\pi {(\\frac{C}{2\\pi })}^{2}=\\frac{{C}^{2}}{4\\pi }.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating this relationship with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(A) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{C}^{2}}{4\\pi }) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}C}(\\frac{{C}^{2}}{4\\pi }) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{C}{2\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen $r=5\\,\\text{cm},$ $C=2\\pi (5)=10\\pi \\text{ cm}.$ Hence, substituting $\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=-8\\pi $ and $C=10\\pi $, and solving for $\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-8\\pi  & =\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{10\\pi }{2\\pi } \\\\ -8\\pi  & =\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot 5 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t} & =-\\frac{8\\pi }{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the circumference is decreasing at a rate of $\\frac{8\\pi }{5}\\text{ cm/s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-2870/ma-source-field/99549ef511efc310e19a15f08816b80b0b4533f3f9dd090f620d4e12fe4fee4c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
