 {:db/id "q-29664/ma-source-field/161a4147179d5992442a3587de65a2157d710f884a1dbeffc321d697b0ef16a9" :answer-field/id #uuid "4440a234-4417-5c7c-aab8-361ac22515f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-29664/ma-source-field/161a4147179d5992442a3587de65a2157d710f884a1dbeffc321d697b0ef16a9/c3e74ce6fba7b7bd77c7afbf20a82e8f73f6cac3363858b8840c65664e418e03" "q-29664/ma-source-field/161a4147179d5992442a3587de65a2157d710f884a1dbeffc321d697b0ef16a9/93ba270014b2121e0d07324bf08630808d6ed9bfb1e523439708be4e1492051c" "q-29664/ma-source-field/161a4147179d5992442a3587de65a2157d710f884a1dbeffc321d697b0ef16a9/5172a7fa160e878951e4187c255e106b57da0d14098cfe25d30cce3dbd3535c3" "q-29664/ma-source-field/161a4147179d5992442a3587de65a2157d710f884a1dbeffc321d697b0ef16a9/48ed8822e91c61d2180f4e9f6c1b03af7fc6ed780f3ab54702820deafad2d24e" "q-29664/ma-source-field/161a4147179d5992442a3587de65a2157d710f884a1dbeffc321d697b0ef16a9/af3979f69e3c75cfe7f3145a4d599cb170a6cd2ea2b65bc8aeb427117c37252c"] :answer-field/correct "q-29664/ma-source-field/161a4147179d5992442a3587de65a2157d710f884a1dbeffc321d697b0ef16a9/48ed8822e91c61d2180f4e9f6c1b03af7fc6ed780f3ab54702820deafad2d24e" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-29664" :question/id #uuid "0fa4866c-44a3-53be-9ea4-1b3c073da31b" :question/math-academy-id "q-29664" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=-\\frac{3}{4}$ for $-{180}^{∘}<x<{180}^{∘},$ what is the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to the nearest integer?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-\\frac{4}{3}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{4}{3})=(-53.130\\,1…)^{∘}≈-{53.130}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $-{53.130}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-{53.130}^{∘}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add and subtract integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={180}^{∘}+x={180}^{∘}-{53.130}^{∘}={126.870}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $x=-{53.130}^{∘},{126.870}^{∘}.$\n\nFinally, the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ is \n\n$$\n-53.130\\cdot 126.870≈-6\\,741\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-29664/ma-source-field/161a4147179d5992442a3587de65a2157d710f884a1dbeffc321d697b0ef16a9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
