 {:db/id "q-37180/ma-source-field/46b2cfa9491114d88b804ad669fcbf2950ce5bc72fc4649eb8f7843dcfa60350" :answer-field/id #uuid "f34c38b1-0c67-5df9-bd25-f72ef39097ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-37180/ma-source-field/46b2cfa9491114d88b804ad669fcbf2950ce5bc72fc4649eb8f7843dcfa60350/5f0a71d842ee5c32d48b20272af32a240f9b54f86154740c26f11f2bc83f53d7" "q-37180/ma-source-field/46b2cfa9491114d88b804ad669fcbf2950ce5bc72fc4649eb8f7843dcfa60350/38d9b4a80e5c36380af5db5802ed305f28716ddc3b8e505e257a56860c5e8b5a" "q-37180/ma-source-field/46b2cfa9491114d88b804ad669fcbf2950ce5bc72fc4649eb8f7843dcfa60350/a34c654dcac9001f079ec25779eac0f8058d7e177e2ae93929dc4dcc6593bbe6" "q-37180/ma-source-field/46b2cfa9491114d88b804ad669fcbf2950ce5bc72fc4649eb8f7843dcfa60350/8ddaaa3c22c182078534a19f8f7ed63f84d580d196766a60c493201bcad522d9" "q-37180/ma-source-field/46b2cfa9491114d88b804ad669fcbf2950ce5bc72fc4649eb8f7843dcfa60350/68057005a1a5d1829183e2576095ff2c02215b574ddfcb08e8b9d3897f2d661f"] :answer-field/correct "q-37180/ma-source-field/46b2cfa9491114d88b804ad669fcbf2950ce5bc72fc4649eb8f7843dcfa60350/38d9b4a80e5c36380af5db5802ed305f28716ddc3b8e505e257a56860c5e8b5a" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-37180" :question/id #uuid "6960a095-e760-5362-9086-48e7e2e653fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-37180" :question/problem "Which of the following initial value problems is an inhibited growth problem?" :question/worked-solution "An inhibited growth initial value problem has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=k(a-y),\\,y(0)={y}_{0}\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>y$ for all $t\\ge 0.$\n\nFrom the given options, the only inhibited growth problem is\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=12\\,510-18P,\\,P(0)=690,\n$$\n\nsince\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=12\\,510-18P=18(695-P).\n$$\n\nIn this case, $k=18,a=695,$ and ${y}_{0}=690.$ Notice that $a>{y}_{0},$ which is required for inhibited growth. \n\nThe other options do not represent inhibited growth. In particular, the initial value problems\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=16\\,256-4P=4(4\\,064-P),\\,P(0)=4\\,070,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=2\\,580-0.6P=0.6(4\\,300-P),\\,P(0)=4\\,400\n$$\n\ndo *not* represent an inhibited growth model because ${y}_{0}=4\\,070>a=4\\,064,$ and ${y}_{0}=4\\,400>a=4\\,300.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-37180/ma-source-field/46b2cfa9491114d88b804ad669fcbf2950ce5bc72fc4649eb8f7843dcfa60350"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
