 {:db/id "q-38012" :question/id #uuid "4809e77f-c615-585e-bbe9-4304896c33b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-38012" :question/problem "The linear transformation $T$ and the vector $b\\in {R}^{4}$ are given below. Determine if there exists a vector $x\\in {R}^{4}$ such that $T(x)=b.$\nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{4},$ where ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3},{x}_{4}$ are the components of $x.$  \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+2{x}_{4}+2{x}_{3} \\\\ 5{x}_{2}-7{x}_{4}-3{x}_{1}-{x}_{3} \\\\ 4{x}_{2}+{x}_{4}+5{x}_{3}+2{x}_{1} \\\\ -7{x}_{3}-{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-{x}_{4}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write down the standard matrix of $T:$\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -1 & -7 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -7 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSince $T$ is the standard matix of $T,$ we have $\\text{Im}(T)=\\text{Col}(T).$ In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Im}(T),$ we need to check if the equation $Tx=b$ is consistent. \n\nSo, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[T\\,|\\,b]$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -1 & -7 & -8 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 5 & 1 & -9 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -7 & -1 & 10\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 1 & -3 & -15 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -5 & 1 & 13\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -14 & 0 & -18 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 14\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the foruth equation, we get the false statement $0=14.$ Therefore, the system is inconsistent, and we conclude that  $b\\notin \\text{Im}(T).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-38012/ma-source-field/d328ecd9381f2f32f2a132434ee9892e21ef9c9c1871cf57d462d6a1ef783a37"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
