 {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "2125dbf2-368d-5ee6-b919-9a772694e1b8"] :question/problem "Calculate the points where the hyperbola $9{x}^{2}-16{y}^{2}=144$ intersects the line $x=5.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $x=5,$ we substitute $x=5$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}^{2}-16{y}^{2} & =144 \\\\ 9(5)^{2}-16{y}^{2} & =144 \\\\ -16{y}^{2} & =144-225 \\\\ -16{y}^{2} & =-81 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =\\frac{81}{16} \\\\ y & =\\pm \\frac{9}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the hyperbola intersects the vertical line $x=5$ at the points $(5,\\pm \\frac{9}{4}).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-8005/ma-source-field/f281d1d76b77551afb40ede7a71403b2a1734493c7d841c95e4b14deb413822f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
